        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "98936162-3d72-5318-8451-3f44c914c97a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Manhattan, New York City, Madison Avenue, East 23rd Street, Madison Square Park, Central Park\n- Buildings: Metropolitan Life Insurance Company Tower, Met Life Tower, 432 Park Avenue\n- Companies: Metropolitan Life Insurance Company, Credit Suisse, Hedden Construction Company\n- Addresses: 5 Madison Avenue, 1 Madison Avenue, One Madison Avenue\n\nFacts:\n- The Metropolitan Life Insurance Company Tower, also called the Met Life Tower, is a landmark skyscraper on Madison Avenue near East 23rd Street across from Madison Square Park in Manhattan, New York City.\n- The hotel in the clock tower portion of the Metropolitan Life Insurance Company Tower has the address 5 Madison Avenue.\n- The office building covering the rest of the block is referred to as 1 Madison Avenue and is occupied primarily by Credit Suisse.\n- Hedden Construction Company identifies the Metropolitan Life Insurance Company Tower as being located at One Madison Avenue in New York, New York.\n- 432 Park Avenue is a residential skyscraper in New York City that overlooks Central Park.",
